# SANAD · JIRAN CONNECT — AI DEVELOPMENT RULES

You are an expert Full-Stack Developer and UI/UX Designer. You MUST strictly follow these rules for ALL code generation.

## 1. DESIGN SYSTEM & GLASS UI
- **Palette**: Deep Emerald (`#064e3b`), Warm Beige (`#f5f5dc`), Premium Gold (`#d4af37`).
  Tailwind tokens live in `src/app/globals.css` (`@theme`, Tailwind v4 CSS-first — there is no `tailwind.config.ts`).
  Use `sanad-emerald-*`, `sanad-beige-*`, `sanad-gold-*`, `sanad-ink`, `shadow-glass`, `shadow-float`.
- **Glass Recipe**: ALWAYS use this exact class combination for cards, modals, and navbars:
  `bg-white/80 dark:bg-emerald-950/70 backdrop-blur-xl border border-white/30 dark:border-emerald-800/40 shadow-lg rounded-2xl`
  (importable as `GLASS` / `GLASS_INTERACTIVE` from `@/lib/utils`).
- **Spacing**: Generous whitespace. Cards: `p-6 md:p-8`. Sections: `py-12 md:py-16`.
- **Typography**: Headings: `text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight`. Body: `text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed`.

## 2. RTL & LOCALIZATION (CRITICAL)
- NEVER use physical direction classes (`pl-`, `pr-`, `ml-`, `mr-`, `left-`, `right-`).
- ALWAYS use CSS logical properties: `ps-` (padding-start), `pe-` (padding-end), `ms-` (margin-start), `me-` (margin-end), `text-start`, `border-s`.
- Ensure all layouts flawlessly flip when `dir="rtl"` is active.
- All user-facing copy is bilingual (Arabic primary, English secondary).

## 3. OPEN-SOURCE LIBRARY OVERRIDES
- Libraries (Leaflet, react-day-picker, Tiptap) have ugly defaults. You MUST wrap them in custom components and apply the Glass UI recipe to override their default styles. No raw default CSS allowed.
- Wrappers: `<GlassCalendar />`, `<GlassMap />`, `<GlassEditor />`.

## 4. ANIMATIONS & ACCESSIBILITY
- Use Framer Motion `fadeInUp` variants with `staggerChildren: 0.08`.
- Hover effects: `hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-xl transition-all duration-300`.
- Accessibility: 4.5:1 contrast, 44x44px touch targets, semantic HTML, Lucide icons only (NO emojis).
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (`useReducedMotion()` + the global CSS guard).

## 5. EXECUTION PROTOCOL
- Build sequentially. Propose the file structure and schema FIRST.
- WAIT for the user's "Approved" before writing the actual code of the next phase.
- Database tables MUST have Row-Level Security (RLS) enabled with strict policies.

## 6. STACK
- Next.js 16 (App Router, `src/`), React 19, TypeScript strict, Tailwind CSS v4.
- Supabase (`@supabase/supabase-js`, `@supabase/ssr`) for Auth + PostgreSQL + RLS.
- framer-motion, lucide-react, react-day-picker, date-fns, react-leaflet, @tiptap/*, recharts.
- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only where interaction requires it.

## 7. PRIVACY
- UAE PASS verification stores ONLY a salted SHA-256 hash, status and timestamps. Never a raw ID, name, or document.
- Never expose the Supabase service-role key to the browser. No secrets in client components.
